Lock reason:
During the audit completed on site on 06/05/2025 the following Major NCs and KO were identified:
 3.2.2 KO: The HACCP/Quality Manager C.A. does not wear the clothing and headgear required by internal procedures during the tour of the production premises.. Also, presence of employee with false eyelashes detected in production premises, although company procedure POG1 Internal personnel rules ed. 0 rev. 1 of 2024/03/04 reports this prohibition. The employee is not directly involved in production.
 4.9.2.2 MAJOR: 1) In the product reception area there is an opening for the passage of a fire pipe that does not adhere to the pipe itself. 2) In the product reception area there is an almond peeling machine next to a wall with a noticeable peeling of paint. The peeling machine is open, the product is on display.
 4.10.2 MAJOR: During the visit to the production premises found the following situations of non-compliant hygiene: 1) Presence of cobwebs in the production room, raw material and finished product storage area, and staff rooms. 2) dusty aerial parts (pipes, ducts, neon) in the production department and storage rooms. 3) containers containing bulk products (pistachio and shelled almonds), present in raw material storage cell and finished product storage area, dirty in visible parts. 4) equipment with residues from previous processing (inside of packaging machine funnels, surfaces in contact with conveyor belts). 5) In raw materials receiving area found presence of an inadequately cleaned almond peeling machine with residues from previous processing and a couple of kilograms of almond product left on the belts. Also present accumulation of product from previous processing on the floor below the peeler. The company initially stated that this was machine no longer in use. 6) corners of the floor in raw material receiving area and in finished product storage area, with accumulation of dust and dirt in corners 7) insect nets soiled with dusty residue in product packaging room.
 4.12.1 KO Insufficient procedures were adopted to prevent the risk of contamination of the product by foreign bodies. During the inspection, the following situations of risk of contamination by foreign bodies were found:
 • presence of wooden pallets in the raw material cell (due to overlapping of big bags) near uncovered product present in crates;
 • use of adhesive tape and cardboard for temporary repairs on the 3 packaging machines and on the sorter in operation;
 • presence of a container for raw material to be processed with loss of coating paint;
 • use of wooden stools and tables in the production departments to support material, even if intact;
 • repair with scotch tape on sewing machine for product bags;
 • in the packaging room presence of maintenance equipment, spare parts for the machine and small parts (screws and bolts) on a low wall behind the packaging machine;
 • for peeling machine present in the reception area, presence of scotch tape was detected on two control/electrical panels;
 • presence of two knives with plastic handles detected, one in the reception area and one in the packaging area, used in place of the fixed blade knives supplied to staff;
 • presence in the overhead areas (ceiling) of non-metal detectable cable ties for securing overhead cables and pipes;
 • presence of operating instructions fixed with scotch tape in the finished product storage area"
 4.13.1 MAJOR The premises and equipment at the site are not fully designed and maintained to prevent pest infestation as required by the requirement. Specifically: 1) There are two swinging doors with bottom seals that are not fully intact and the door leaf leaves a gap that potentially allows pests to enter. 2) One automatic door does not fully close all the way to the floor. The automatic door is placed immediately after one of the two swing doors and marks the entrance to production. Immediately after the door, on the right wall, detected UV lamp No. 34 with the glue panel almost completely covered with plodia and other flying insects, less than 24 hours after the monitoring intervention carried out by the external company responsible for the service. 3) There is a hole in the wall in the goods entry area, from which outside light is visible. 4) A window in the packaging area has damaged mosquito netting. 5) In product packaging area there is a portion of the wall, which in the lower part consists of a small wall covered in a non-smooth manner, with the presence of small holes. Leaning against the small wall is an insulation board that leaves a space of a few millimeters free from the small wall. Accumulated dust and dead insects are present in the space indicated. Since this is a packaging department, there is product and packaging on display.
 4.14.3 MAJOR In packaging room, coils are stored resting directly on the floor, also present partially used coils, not covered after use. Also present, in finished product storage room, plastic buckets that the company declares not to be used, resting on the floor, not properly covered, with presence of dust and dead insects (plodie), also lacking any indication of traceability.
 5.11.3 KO Corrective actions related to last year's IFS audit were not effectively closed, specifically related to items: 2.3.5.1 The flowchart validation report conducted on 2025/01/08 does not include a clear reference to product in production during validation. 4.9.2.3 Detected missing portions of skirting board in packaging area, dressing room, finished product storage area. 4.9.3.1 Detected portion of tile floor not intact in raw material and packaging receiving area. 4.9.6.2 Raw materials and packaging entry hatch has damaged brushes in several places, absence of brushes at joint points, and gap with respect to flooring at the side. The door at the opposite side of the room has ruined brushes in several places and absence of brushes at the junction points. In addition, the automatic roll-up door protecting the production entrance does not close perfectly at the bottom, leaving a gap of several centimeters open. 4.12.3 Detected in packaging room, on small table behind packaging machine, a package of non-segregated alcohol with broken cap not allowing the package to close. 4.13.5 In raw material storage cell detected presence of unidentified pest monitoring trap. At the exit of the same cell, on pilsatro placed on the right, detected presence of an identification sign with numbering 33 without the presence of a corresponding trap. 4.16.5 Detected temporary repairs with tape and cardboard on the 3 packing machines and the sorting machine in operation. Repairs are placed in such places as to come in contact with the product (e.g., product passage or exit areas) 4.10.2 Packaging machines, including conveyor belts carrying unpacked product and loading tanks have residues of previous processing.

As of today (02.07.2025) Certima BV withdraw the certificate number IFS-01118 of client

 Energique B.V.
 Wetterkant 10, 8401GC Gorredijk, Netherlands
 COID: 62626

 Reason: During the audit conducted in period 23-25.06.2025, the auditor raised multiple Major and KO non-conformities.

 1.2.1 KO: Based on the site tour observations and the samples of documents and records reviewed during the audit it can be concluded the company’s management does not guarantee that employees know and implement their responsibilities. In the course of the audit a large number of critical non-conformities were found.

 1.2.2 Major: During the first day of the audit 3 different sausage-type products were in production, own brand RAW. One of the product had declared on the packaging a net weight of 450 g, marked with the ‘e’-sign. According to the local legislation, the company is required to have a formal approval by the government control authority to use the e-sign on pre-packed products. Currently the company does not hold such official approval.

 4.12.1 KO: During the site tour there were several observations where the risk of products’ contamination with foreign materials could not be excluded:
 - in the cooling chamber for meat ingredients thawing there were several pallets where products were in direct contact with wooden pallets that were in poor condition, including splintering parts; one of the pallets was colored with red paint, the company representatives could not explain what kind of paint this is, it was not clear whether it is suitable for direct contact with the meat products;
 - in the frozen storage chamber on number of pallets splinters of wood were seen (from the pallets stored on upper level racks);
 - during the visit in the meat preparation area cleaning between two batches (charges) in the meat grinder was observed; the operator was cleaning the floor and moving the floor water to the near drain, on the way back where cleaning tools are stored, the floor squeegee that was just used, was moved right above a pallet with open product prepared for the next meat mixing;
 - further cleaning operations in the same area executed in unhygienic way were observed – operator picking waste from the floor and handing it out to another operator, touching and moving the floor drain grid and further manipulation with products without changing gloves or hands washing;
 - during the visit in the production area, sausage line, on the casing filing machine, above the open feeding hopper, the motor of the near screw conveyor was seen rusty, with flaking paint;
 - the inside of the freezing tunnel was inspected after the machine has been cleaned – seen rusty grids on the fans, loose sealing between the wall and the ceiling, a built up of product residues on the bottom side of the conveyor;

 4.18.1 KO: 1) During the first day of the audit a traceability exercise was executed on product RAW Veterinary Diets Hypoallergenic 12 x 450 g, PD 31.03.2025, LOT B14-25, 2986.2 kg. The presented production documents show two charges of meat ingredients (1241 kg & 1221 kg) and two charges of dry and liquid ingredients have been prepared (1005 kg), to a total quantity of 3405 kg of semi-finished product before filling into casings. From the production records presented the total quantity of final products produced is 3069 kg. However the difference in the quantity of about 400 kg of prepared material before filling and after filling in cases could not be traced on the provided records and the company could not explain or identify that remaining material.
 2) During the site tour in the packaging storage area pre-printed labels were seen present. These bear the legally-required information for the products. These labels are not covered by the implemented traceability system – their usage is not recorded.

 5.10.1 Major: During the audit different products and materials were seen marked as blocked – e.g. final products planned for products for rework, raw materials, products blocked during the audit related to observed non-conformities. Besides the pallets being marked as blocked, no further records are kept on what the identified issues are, defined responsibilities, risk assessment or decision about further handling. The possible misuse of non-confirming products can not be excluded as there is no traceable data on the status of the non-conforming products.

The company Mar Cabo - Produtos Congelados Lda - COID 71826 received a authority visit (DGAV) on July 03, 2025, the report was released and sent to WQS last week. 
 24 Non-conformities were raised which the following below show that there are products at risk and/or legal requirements are not met (for example): 

 e) The walls and ceiling of the access corridor to chambers CAM 01, CAM 02, and CAM 03 had several dark spots consistent with the presence of mold; 
 f) In chamber CAM 03, water dripping from the evaporator was visible, but the product underneath was properly protected. 
 h) The ceiling of the Sector II freezing tunnel had condensation, and underneath there was product that was not properly protected; 
 3) In the Sector II production room, some knives with orange stains consistent with oxidation were observed inside the container for clean and sanitized knives. There were also knives with moisture on them, which is not in accordance with the utensil cleaning and disinfection plan, which states that utensils must be properly dried after sanitization. It was also found that there are no provisions for intermediate sanitization of knives used in filleting operations during the work period. All of this is in breach of the provisions of Article 5 and paragraph 1 of Chapter V of Annex II, both of Regulation (EC) No. 852/4 of April 29. 

 With regard to the assessment of specific requirements for export to the Federative Republic of Brazil, the following was verified: 
 I. With regard to Standard Operating Hygiene Procedures (PPHO), there is no defined and implemented plan establishing daily hygiene actions for facilities, equipment, utensils, and manufacturing practices carried out during intra-operational periods, complemented by specific requirements such as monitoring, verification, application of corrective measures, and respective records, in violation of the provisions of Article 54 of Chapter II of Title IV of Decree No. 9,013 of March 29, 2017; 
 II. Regarding “Work Instruction IFS-GP.01.15 v4.24,” with respect to "Quality Control – Parasites”, the document presented does not define the criteria for acceptability in fish, nor does it refer to another document that allows compliance with Memorandum-Circular No. 2/2018/CGI/DIPOA/MAPA/SDA/MAPA, of February 8, 2018. 

 The company has lost the license to export products to Brazil, Argentina, Cuba and Colombia.

Following an epidemiological investigation, the health authorities (DDPP, DGAL/MUS) have established that the company is involved in cases of listeriosis in France and Europe (cluster 714).
 This resulted in recalls on June 13, 2025, and August 9, 2025, linked to the detection of Listeria monocytogenes in a pasteurized soft cheese.
 In accordance with the IFS Food standard, we suspend the certification with effect from August 22, 2025. Following an audit carried out on the premises on August 27, 2025, a decision was taken to lift the suspension on the basis of the action plan that was being implemented. 

 A number of events then took place, including:
 - a fire in part of premises (Goat workshop), following which, in accordance with the IFS standard, we had to inform the certification scheme prescriber and reduce your certification scope on October 14, 2025;
 - a formal notice issued to the company by the Creuse DDETSPP (Departmental Directorate for Employment, Labor, Social Protection, and Professional Training) to carry out actions following its visit on September 4 and 5, 2025, which were to be completed before November 13, 2025, and week 49;
 - unsatisfactory results of the analysis of samples relating to Listeria monocytogenes and Listeria spp in your company's production environment (no contamination identified in finished products) according to the documents sent in December 2025;
 - the information sent to the company by the Creuse DDETSPP on 21/01/2026 stating that the Listeria monocytogenes genosero group detected in the production environment corresponds to that of cluster 714 (IVb / serovar 4b or 4d or 4 e);
 - new unsatisfactory results from the analysis of samples relating to Listeria monocytogenes in the production environment (ripening room 19 and molding machine), leading to two notifications to the authorities according to the documents sent on January 27, 2026;
 - A search of the premises on January 27, 2026, as part of the ongoing judicial investigation;
 - a request by the Creuse DDETSPP (Departmental Directorate for Employment, Labor, Social Protection, and Population) to the company, dated February 2, 2026, for additional information as soon as possible, following the notification from its services on January 28, 2026, to which a response was made on February 5, 2026;
 - the notification by the DDETSPP of Creuse to the company, dated February 5, 2026, of a proposed suspension of health approval indicating, among other things, insufficient action in the updated health control plan, which was also assessed as incomplete, and informing of a new human case of listeriosis detected in November 2025 (cluster 714) and the failure to lift the formal notices, the proposed suspension of approval relating to milk processing, which corresponds to the scope of your certification according to the IFS standard;
 - similarity of the strains isolated in the environment to the strains in cluster 714, according to the information provided on February 6, 2026.
 In view of the above events, which show in particular the recurrent detection of Listeria monocytogenes in the direct and indirect production environment, we hereby suspend certification according to the IFS Food standard.
 This suspension takes effect on 02/13/2026

During the audit completed on site on 03/02/2026 the following KO was identified at requirement 5.9.2:

 As a consequence of the deviations identified during the previous IFS Logistics v3 audit carried out
 on 02/04/25, the company proposed a robust corrective action plan. However, during the on-site
 visit and the review of documentation, it was not possible to verify that the actions related to the
 following requirements had been implemented:
 1.1.1, regarding the implementation of the food safety culture plan;
 4.3.1, regarding the segregation of food products and marketing materials;
 4.8.1, regarding the presence of wood splinters;
 5.8.3, regarding the identification of non-conforming product.
 As a consequence of this situation, the same deviations have been repeated.

